Run the EEVDF core regression tests from the source tree:

    python3 tools/test/sched_eevdf/eevdf_test.py
    CC=clang python3 tools/test/sched_eevdf/eevdf_test.py --sanitize

The runner extracts the actual scheduler functions into a temporary C
translation unit and supplies a deterministic kernel-service fixture.
It requires Python 3 and a C compiler; --sanitize also requires compiler
support for AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.

Checks include the reduced RB deletion regression, randomized red-black
and subtree-minimum invariants, exhaustive eligible-deadline selection,
proportional CPU service, lag and request preservation, large virtual-time
origins, class changes, priority inheritance, renice, migration, wakeup
preemption, non-FIFO quanta, RR interval conversion, and CPU-use decay.

The thread, mutex, bitmap queue, and clock services are fixtures.  These
tests do not exercise hardware context switching or concurrent CPUs and
must be supplemented by kernel builds and workloads on FreeBSD.
